# Rate limiting — plan

Per-user rolling-window throttle for update methods. Goal: cut abuse cheaply and
minimally, with no new infra and no external cache.

## Why

There is no rate limiting in the canister today (`Config.mo` has no throttle
constants, no `rateLimit`/`cooldown` logic exists under `src/`). Every caller-
guarded update call burns cycles and can write state. A scripted principal can
spam paid paths (`purchaseUsername`, `launchToken`, `transfer*`, `withdraw`) and
cheap writes (`updateUsername`, `updateSettings`) to waste cycles and hammer the
ledger canisters.

**Key IC facts that shape the design:**
- **Queries are free.** Only `update` calls need throttling, so the state is
  small and the win is concentrated on the paid/spammy paths.
- **`Time.now()` is monotone across rounds** and constant within a round — fine
  as the window clock.
- **An external cache (Redis etc.) is impossible in Motoko.** A canister is
  isolated; there is no cheaper or external store. An in-canister stable map is
  the only option and is exactly the minimal one.

## Design (minimal, layered)

A rolling **sliding-window** counter per caller. State is a stable map
`Principal -> { windowStart: Int; count: Nat }`, mirrored exactly on the
existing `settings` pattern (`storage -> repository -> service`).

Helper (in a service): given a policy `{ maxPerWindow: Nat; windowSeconds: Nat }`,
```
allow(limits, key, policy, now) : Bool
```
- If no entry → start window at `now`, count = 1, allow.
- If entry is within the window (`now - windowStart < windowSeconds`) →
  increment; allow while `count <= maxPerWindow`.
- If entry is stale (`now - windowStart >= windowSeconds`) → reset window,
  count = 1, allow.

When it returns `false`, the API returns
`#err("Rate limit exceeded. Retry in <seconds>.")`.

The counter is per **principal** (the effective caller), not per method, unless
a method needs its own budget — so one busy user cannot starve others.

## What gets throttled

Only caller-guarded **update** methods. Queries and operator/controller funcs
are untouched.

| Update method | Policy (tune later) | Why |
|---|---|---|
| `launchToken` | 1 / hour | 5 ICP; single attempt per window is enough, pre-fee floods waste cycles |
| `purchaseUsername` | 3 / minute | the paid buy — double-spend / price-point abuse |
| `register` | 5 / minute | username claim |
| `updateUsername` | 5 / minute | username claim path |
| `transferByAccountId` | 5 / minute | repeated transfer attempts |
| `transferByUsername` | 5 / minute | same |
| `transferByPrincipal` | 5 / minute | same |
| `transferByAccount` | 5 / minute | same |
| `withdraw` | 5 / minute | paid withdraw |
| `syncDeposits` | 10 / minute | hits the ledger index canister — real cost |
| `updateSettings` | 10 / 5 min | cheap but writes state |

**Do NOT throttle:** `Admin*`, `Token` operator funcs (`reserveUsername`,
`sealTokenWasm`, `sweepTokenRevenue`, `refreshLedgers`, `releaseFailedCanister`,
`registerLaunchedLedgers`, `topUpToken`, `reserveTokenSymbol`,
`uploadTokenWasmChunk`) — ops/controller paths owned by the CLI.

## Files to add

```
src/storage/RateLimitStorage.mo        # the stable map type + constructor
src/repositories/RateLimitRepository.mo # get / bump / reset (leaf, no logic)
src/services/RateLimitService.mo        # the allow() helper + policies
src/config/Config.mo                    # policy constants (optional single home)
src/main.mo                             # wire the map + pass into services
```

## Storage — `src/storage/RateLimitStorage.mo`

```motoko
import Map "mo:core/Map";

module {
  public type Window = { var windowStart: Int; var count: Nat };
  public type RateLimitMap = Map.Map<Principal, Window>;

  public func createRateLimitMap(): RateLimitMap {
    Map.empty<Principal, Window>();
  };
};
```
`Principal` uses the implicit `Hash`/`Bool` compare in `mo:core/Map`, so no
explicit compare arg is needed — same as `settings.get(userId)` (Text).

## Repository — `src/repositories/RateLimitRepository.mo`

```motoko
import Map "mo:core/Map";
import Principal "mo:core/Principal";

module {
  public func get(limits: RateLimitMap, key: Principal): ?Window {
    limits.get(key);
  };

  public func put(limits: RateLimitMap, key: Principal, w: Window) {
    limits.swap(key, w);
  };
};
```
Note: `Map.add` only inserts **absent** keys, so a reset/rewrite of an existing
entry must use **`swap`** — never `add`. New entries are created by the service
via `put` after building the window.

## Service — `src/services/RateLimitService.mo`

```motoko
import Principal "mo:core/Principal";
import Time "mo:core/Time";
import Nat64 "mo:core/Nat64";
import RateLimitRepo "../repositories/RateLimitRepository";
import RateLimitStorage "../storage/RateLimitStorage";

module {
  public type Policy = { maxPerWindow: Nat; windowSeconds: Nat64 };

  // `now` is nanoseconds from Time.now(), `windowSeconds` is Nat64 so a policy
  // written as a plain literal (e.g. 60) type-checks without a cast.
  public func allow(
    limits: RateLimitStorage.RateLimitMap,
    key: Principal,
    policy: Policy,
    now: Int,
  ): Bool {
    let windowNanos = Int.abs(Nat64.toInt(policy.windowSeconds)) * 1_000_000_000;
    switch (RateLimitRepo.get(limits, key)) {
      case (null) {
        RateLimitRepo.put(limits, key, {
          var windowStart = now;
          var count = 1;
        });
        true;
      };
      case (?w) {
        if (now - w.windowStart >= windowNanos) {
          w.windowStart := now;
          w.count := 1;
          true;
        } else if (w.count < policy.maxPerWindow) {
          w.count += 1;
          true;
        } else {
          false;
        };
      };
    };
  };
};
```

## Call-site shape (service)

Guard at the top of the mutation, before any ledger/write work:

```motoko
// inside e.g. UsernameSaleService.purchaseUsername
if (not RateLimitService.allow(service.limits, caller, Policy.purchase, Time.now())) {
  return #err("Rate limit exceeded. Please retry shortly.");
};
```

## main.mo wiring — must be persistent

Add the map alongside the other stable variables (NOT inside a `transient`
service, or it resets on every upgrade):

```motoko
let rateLimits = RateLimitStorage.createRateLimitMap();
```

then pass `rateLimits` into each mutating service's `create(...)`. Service
records gain one field, e.g. `limits: RateLimitStorage.RateLimitMap`.

## Response shape

Additive — existing endpoints keep their `Types.ApiResult<...>` shape. A hit
simply returns `#err(...)` with a human-readable retry hint; the frontend
`services/` layer already maps `#err(Text)`, so no API contract breaks.

## Edge cases / notes

- **Controller calls bypass** — apply the guard only on caller paths that need
  it; ops funcs stay ungated (they are CLI-owned).
- **Upgrade resets counters** unless the map is persistent — that is acceptable
  (mostly a one-time reset after a deploy) and not a security hole.
- **Single shared window per principal** vs per-method: start shared for
  minimal state; give `launchToken` its own 1/hour window so an active user is
  not blocked from other ops.
- Policies are starting points — tune after observing cycle burn. Keep them in
  `Config.mo` so they compile down to one place.
